cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EquationBench, please cite this benchmark and its version."
title: "EquationBench Linear: An Open-Ended Frontier Benchmark for Exact Linear-System Reasoning"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "EquationBench Contributors"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/equationbench/equationbench"
url: "https://github.com/equationbench/equationbench"
abstract: >-
  EquationBench Linear is a closed-book benchmark of dense integer linear
  systems with exact ground truth. Tasks are generated on an open-ended
  geometric ladder of system sizes, and models are scored by the 50% frontier:
  the largest system they solve reliably. Because the ladder extends, the score
  has no fixed ceiling.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - benchmark
  - linear systems
  - exact arithmetic
  - frontier evaluation
  - leaderboard
